Package: Geneland
Title: Clustering of Living Organisms from Geo-Referenced Genetic and
    Morphometric Data
Version: 5.0.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Gilles",
           family = "Guillot",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "gilles.b.guillot@gmail.com",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0675-8325"))
Description: Bayesian models and Markov chain Monte Carlo algorithms for the
    inference of population genetic structure from geo-referenced individual
    multi-locus genotypes and quantitative phenotypes. Individuals are
    clustered into populations whose spatial extent is modelled by a coloured
    Poisson-Voronoi tessellation. Allele frequencies may be treated as
    independent across populations or as correlated through a common ancestral
    population.
